From cd72cd06b162d818524796b16e2bbfa70b4b4df0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:27:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stm32-rtc: align shadow-register timeout with other
 RTC syncs

0005-stm32-stgen-read-rtc-before-disabling-counter-on-suspend.patch
fixed the silent infinite hang during poweroff by reading the RTC
calendar before disabling the counter its own timeout depends on
- but on hardware this surfaced a second, real issue: the wait
for the RTC ICSR_RSF ("registers synchronized") flag now
correctly times out instead of hanging, and does so, panicking
at stm32_rtc_read_calendar().

stm32_rtc_read_calendar() budgets only TIMEOUT_US_RTC_SHADOW
(10ms) for this wait - the only call site of that constant in
the driver. stm32_rtc_wait_sync(), elsewhere in this same file,
waits on the identical RTC_ICSR_RSF condition and budgets
TIMEOUT_US_RTC_GENERIC (100ms) instead. Align the two: use the
same, already-proven 100ms budget for both RSF waits rather than
an inconsistent, unusually tight one for this path only.

Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c b/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
index a900b979a..5522eec2b 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@
 		/* Wait calendar registers are ready */
 		io_clrbits32(rtc_base + RTC_ICSR, RTC_ICSR_RSF);
 
-		to = timeout_init_us(TIMEOUT_US_RTC_SHADOW);
+		to = timeout_init_us(TIMEOUT_US_RTC_GENERIC);
 		while (!(io_read32(rtc_base + RTC_ICSR) & RTC_ICSR_RSF))
 			if (timeout_elapsed(to))
 				break;
--
